RISC3D test kit 33 (prototype, 15 November 2026)
================================================

Kit 32's results: with rol-3d 0.18's fix and fog off, TORCS draws
right (ReplayNoFog). So the Pi's Mesa (25.0.7) has a second trigger:
lit texture coordinates are also lost when fog is on. A lone normal
(not in an array) breaks the lit colour too.

Mesa's release notes since 25.0.7 list fixes in this very area (the
fixed-function vertex program was rewritten in 25.0; V3D output and
fog fixes came in 25.1-25.3). Debian has Mesa 25.2 for trixie in
trixie-backports. This kit tries it WITHOUT installing it: the script
downloads the packages, unpacks them into /opt/riscos/gl-test, and
switches backports off again. Your system Mesa is not touched.

Steps
-----
 1. Unzip RISC3DTest into HardDisc4, replacing kit 32.
 2. In RiSH's Root shell (needs the internet, a few minutes):
      sh /riscos/HardDisc4/RISC3DTest/newmesa /riscos/3d/recorded/ctx-477.r3d

Please send
-----------
NewMesaLog and the pictures NewMesa-lit.png, NewMesa-litx.png,
NewMesa-litx2.png, NewMesa-replay-nofix-240.png and
NewMesa-replay-240.png.

If the newer Mesa draws everything right, rol-3d can carry it as its
own private Mesa (it already looks in /opt/riscos/gl first). To remove
the test copy: rm -rf /opt/riscos/gl-test
